; Input capture 1 (PA2) interrupt: crank sensor edge - the main engine position event. [reviewed -
; partially]
;
; Time-stamps the edge (TIC1) and measures it against the last input capture 3 time and the number
; of timer overflows since the previous pulse. Reset programs TCTL2 = $1A: IC1 captures rising
; edges and IC3 falling edges, so TIC1 - TIC3 is the low time before this rising edge. That
; separates the slots inside a group (short low time) from the first edge after the long gap
; between groups. Each group of the crank wheel has four rising edges, one per event phase (see
; docs/en/engine_control.md). When the engine is synchronised (SyncFlags75 bit 5 or 6, depending
; on the phase bit in SyncFlags74 bit 7) it increments CrankEventCounter and calls one of four
; handlers from CrankPickupIntrAddressTable, selected by the low two bits of SyncFlags75:
; CrankInterrupt_FallingEdge, CrankInterrupt_HandleCamSensorRisingEdgeA,
; CrankInterrupt_HandleCamSensorRisingEdgeB and CrankInterrupt_CalculateFuel. Fuel and spark for
; the next cylinder are scheduled from these handlers.
